WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheers)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.430
- I love that we called each other.

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.743
- I know.
- And you wear your black.

00:00:03.743 --> 00:00:04.860
- We're just like that.
- You even put sparkle in it.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.693
I like it.

00:00:05.693 --> 00:00:07.590
You're in a cover band,
so I didn't know this.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.660
- I used to be in a cover band, yeah.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:10.830
- Oh, you don't do it anymore?

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.870
- No, I should get the
band back on the road.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.070
I've been a bit busy.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.420
- I'm making movies.
- I should call up the boys.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.210
- Yeah, 'cause it's all boys.
You were the only girl, right?

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:20.430
- Yeah, I started it
when I was 13 years old.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.872
- Look at you.
- Oh my God. (chuckles)

00:00:21.872 --> 00:00:23.250
- [Studio Audience] Aww.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.930
- I really blinged it out.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.780
- I used to have, like,
three of those hats.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.020
Like, in corduroy, it
was like my favorite.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.720
- Oh my god, those were the go-to.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.670
I probably got it from you.

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.503
- You probably didn't.

00:00:33.503 --> 00:00:35.010
I got it from "Fievel Goes West."

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.830
I got it from a movie
that was long before you.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.630
But I loved that, I didn't
know that about you.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.980
It's interesting that you love music

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.290
and then you end up in
this role, like, Priscilla.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.150
So what was it like, you're
from Missouri, right?

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.460
Coming to Hollywood, that's a difference.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.530
- Oh yeah, that was a
bit of a culture shock.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.910
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.913
It was a crazy sort of
all-American journey.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.090
I was actually performing with the band

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.800
at some fall festival,

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.220
and then I met a guy, who
knew a guy, who knew a guy

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.640
who lived in LA, and we're
like, okay, let's pack the bags.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.890
That was enough for us.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:12.890
It was like a 25-hour drive
cross-country, me and my mom.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.310
- You have super cool parents.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.990
- Yeah, they really supported me.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:16.920
- Yeah.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.500
- Stayed in some random people's-

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.684
- Shady places?
(they chuckle)

00:01:22.684 --> 00:01:24.090
You do what you can, yes.
- Yeah.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:26.190
And so, that was about four years.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.323
We'd make that trip multiple times a year,

00:01:29.278 --> 00:01:31.260
and yeah, four years of nothing, silence,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.225
and I think we were about to give up.

00:01:34.225 --> 00:01:36.600
Then got my first role
the month after I was 18.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.040
- What it like?

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.080
Kind of a perfect time to get
your first role, actually.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:40.913
- I think so, too.

00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:41.746
- To be 18, and being able
to be more independent.

00:01:41.746 --> 00:01:43.350
- I was a little bit older.
- Yeah.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.150
- I felt like that was a
good place to kick it off.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:45.983
- What was it like?

00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:47.310
Were you in Missouri
when you got that call?

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.360
- I was, yeah.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.950
I remember I had bad reception.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.771
I couldn't hear them, like, wh-what?

00:01:51.771 --> 00:01:54.720
It was the last thing, I
thought I'd lost it, you know?

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.860
I thought I blew the audition.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:58.230
And then I went outside on my driveway,

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.540
and then my parents came
out and they were crying,

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.550
and they were recording me on their phone.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.520
I just remember, like, the
whole world was spinning.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.353
- That's fun.

00:02:06.353 --> 00:02:08.520
- I just called every person
I could on my contacts

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.990
to let them know. (chuckles)
- [Studio Audience] Aww.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.400
- That's so exciting.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.770
I did the same thing when I was on a show,

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:15.150
before you were probably born.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.670
But I did, I got so excited.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.510
'Cause it's like your big-

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:19.800
especially if you're from a small town

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:21.189
nowhere near the glitz and the glamour.

00:02:21.189 --> 00:02:22.560
- Yeah, you just wanna
scream on every roof-

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:23.847
- Yeah, a mountaintop.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:23.847 --> 00:02:26.713
- I made it, possibly!
- I did it!

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:27.960
(they chuckle)

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.280
- So Priscilla, I love though,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.660
like I was saying, you're into music,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.970
and you end up like playing
this role, Priscilla,

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:33.803
who was with Elvis.

00:02:33.803 --> 00:02:36.360
What was it like doing this movie?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.910
- Well it was so special
because, you know, growing up,

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.080
I was born in Tennessee,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.700
I was raised in the southern Midwest,

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:44.018
so Elvis was like such
a part of our world.

00:02:44.018 --> 00:02:46.473
We grew up going to Graceland,

00:02:48.094 --> 00:02:49.560
and Elvis and Priscilla are so iconic,

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.820
they're like American royalty.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.160
But I didn't know her side of the story.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.725
- I find that interesting,
I know, I didn't either.

00:02:54.725 --> 00:02:57.175
- I know, that was what
was so exciting about it.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:01.260
I think it's long overdue
to hear her side of things.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.840
- And to see him from a
different vantage point than

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.190
most people got to see him.
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.900
I think Jacob did a beautiful job.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.810
And to have someone like
Sophia Coppola tell this story,

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:13.680
who's got such a grasp of how to tell it

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.390
from the female perspective.

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.440
- Absolutely.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.810
- And she doesn't in such a beautiful way.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:20.280
Her movies are stunning.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:22.410
- They are aesthetically
so, they're like candy.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:23.670
- Yeah, they are, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:27.030
- And that world, that
sixties Americana was so rich,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.640
and the colors fashion and...

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.780
- Yeah, that's awesome.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.612
We had Jacob Elordie here.
I fell in love with him.

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.030
- I know, it's hard not to.
- He's so great.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:37.440
- He's so sweet.
- So sweet.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.080
Little Aussie boy, I was like,
oh my gosh, he's so sweet.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.460
But one of the things that I-

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.140
First of all, how did y'all bond?

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.010
I'll ask that question first,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.810
just 'cause y'all didn't know
each other before this, right?

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.700
So, you're playing these
intimate roles, right?

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.500
- Well, sometimes you get onto set

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.440
and it's okay to meet on day
one, just roll right into it.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.780
But playing Elvis and Priscilla,

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.640
I knew that we had to have that connection

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.260
and had to have that trust in each other.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.330
So, when I found out he got the role,

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.220
I was so excited 'cause I loved his work,

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.320
but I didn't know how he was gonna be.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.330
So I basically emailed him,

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.973
and forced him to hang out
with me and be friends.

00:04:07.973 --> 00:04:08.970
(audience chuckles)
(they chuckle)

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.950
- You will be my friend.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.470
- I was like, do you
wanna go horseback riding?

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.170
'Cause that was something
Elvis and Priscilla loved to do

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.453
and he was so game.
- I love that.

00:04:18.453 --> 00:04:19.286
- Oh yeah, that's-

00:04:19.286 --> 00:04:20.726
- Oh, I've been there, that's on Sunset.

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:21.559
- I know.
- I've done that.

00:04:21.559 --> 00:04:23.040
- And the Hollywood sign?
- Yes!

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.450
- I've been there, that's so awesome.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.040
But it's kind of hard to
have a conversation though.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.570
- Oh yeah, I know, it was so awkward.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.040
He's like behind me riding a horse.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.276
I'm like, so what- Are you
close with your family?

00:04:33.276 --> 00:04:34.500
(they laugh)

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.740
In this, like, group
horseback riding trip.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.030
But he was so great,

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:42.450
and he was so connected with the, the hor-

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.880
like, he's such a outback Australian.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.620
- Oh, like an animal guy.
- Yeah.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:47.453
- I love him.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.620
And one of the things I loved
about him that we found out,

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.810
is he's an amazing photographer.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.280
My favorite picture he took is of you.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.330
I don't know if you've read your card yet,

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:56.070
but I hope you get a copy of it.

00:04:56.070 --> 00:04:57.267
I have to show this picture.
- Oh, I wanna see.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:59.670
- Oh, this is not one I've seen.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.820
No, no, this is beautiful,
I've never seen that one.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.720
It was another one that we showed.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.130
But anyway, we could show it-

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.721
Oh, I've never seen that one either!

00:05:06.721 --> 00:05:09.480
(audience laughs and applauds)

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.430
- They gave us more.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.980
Oh my god, he is such
a great photographer.

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:14.813
- I know, that was so special.

00:05:14.813 --> 00:05:17.940
- There's this one and you
look like a first lady.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.860
It's this one that they
showed whenever he was on.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.960
It's so beautiful, and I just was like,

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.910
I hope you get this picture.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.170
He should send this to you.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.318
This should be your Christmas present.

00:05:26.318 --> 00:05:27.660
- I just love that he did that,

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.150
because we shot the movie in 30 days.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:32.730
So I sort of have amnesia
when I think back on it.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.500
It's so fun to see those photos,

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.767
and it was such a wild
journey we all went on.

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:38.250
- That's a month.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.180
- Yeah, to finish the-
(audience chuckles)

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:40.620
I know, only a month.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.650
- I just got anxiety for
you and it's already done.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.123
I was like, wow, okay.

